      "id": "ru-w4-d22",
      "day": 22,
      "title": "Plans for Tomorrow",
      "focus": "собираться + инфинитив",
      "estimated_minutes": 20,
      "objectives": [
        "talk about immediate future plans",
        "ask what someone is going to do",
        "combine a plan with a time and place"
      ],
      "teaching": {
        "explanation": "The high-frequency future pattern in Russian is собираться + infinitive: я собираюсь учиться, ты собираешься работать, мы собираемся есть. It is more useful at this level than memorizing complex future forms.",
        "pattern": "Я собираюсь учиться завтра. Что ты собираешься делать? = What are you going to do?",
        "note": "The preposition usage differs from Spanish; also note Russian uses informal ты and polite Вы — be aware of register when asking someone about plans."
      },
