      "estimated_minutes": 20,
      "objectives": [
        "recognize essential irregular forms",
        "use у меня есть for possession and basic states",
        "build practical sentences without overgeneralizing regular endings"
      ],
      "teaching": {
        "explanation": "Some of the most useful verbs behave differently in Russian. The verb 'to be' is usually omitted in the present: 'Я студент' (not 'Я есть студент'). For possession use the chunk 'у меня есть'. Learn useful first-person chunks: (identity by noun), я нахожусь, у меня есть, я иду, я делаю. Add the subject only when contrast or emphasis helps.",
        "pattern": "У меня есть время. Я устал/устала. Я иду в кафе. Я задаю вопрос.",
        "note": "Gendered adjectives such as устал/устала should match the speaker; the app should accept both forms where appropriate."
      },
